title: castle_godwin_context
---
// Castle Godwin's staff (the Evil dimension): the people who keep a tyrant's
// castle running, in the kitchens under the gatehouse. One node per resident,
// named `castle_<resident>`.
//
// Everyday talk only (Jon, 2026-10-29: "we are world building not quest
// building"): no flags, no errands.
//
// Never played. No placement names this node; it declares the zone.
===

title: castle_hargreave
---
Mrs Hargreave: Wipe your feet. I do not care whose side you are on, you are not tracking moor into my kitchen.
-> What are you cooking?
    Mrs Hargreave: Gruel. Yesterday it was gruel with a sprig of parsley. The Baron said the parsley was "insubordinate".
    Mrs Hargreave: So it is gruel again. Gruel never contradicted anybody.
-> How long have you worked here?
    Mrs Hargreave: I fed the old Count, and the Count's general, and now the Baron. Three regimes.
    Mrs Hargreave: They come and go. The kitchen stays. Somebody has to do the potatoes after the revolution.
-> Are you evil?
    Mrs Hargreave: I put salt in the soldiers' porridge and none in the officers'. You decide.
-> I will get out of your way.
===

title: castle_osgood
---
Osgood: Name? Purpose of visit? Never mind, write "hero" like the others. The book needs a name, not a truth.
-> What do you do here?
    Osgood: Night porter. I open the gate, I close the gate, I write down who went through it.
    Osgood: Forty years. It has been night for all of them. The day porter, I am told, has an easier time of it.
-> Who else has come through?
    Osgood: A wolf that used to be a man, or the other way round. A ghost who signed twice. A salesman who wanted to sell the Baron a moat.
    Osgood: The Baron already had a moat. He bought a second one. It is behind the first one.
-> Do you ever sleep?
    Osgood: In the day. I am told it is very bright. I keep the curtains shut out of loyalty.
-> Goodnight, Osgood.
    Osgood: It always is.
===

title: castle_dunmore
---
Brigid Dunmore: Brigid Dunmore, shop steward, Henchpersons' Guild, Local Six-Six-Six. You are not management, are you?
-> What does the Guild want?
    Brigid Dunmore: Helmets with eyeholes. A tea break that is longer than the sermon. A pension for anyone the hero throws off a battlement.
    Brigid Dunmore: Management says the helmets are "intimidating". They are. Mostly to the people wearing them.
-> Are you on strike?
    Brigid Dunmore: Work to rule. We march at the speed of the slowest member, and the slowest member is a zombie.
-> Why work for the Baron at all?
    Brigid Dunmore: Rent, mostly. And the Baron's predecessor was worse. Ask Mrs Hargreave, she fed him.
-> Solidarity.
    Brigid Dunmore: Ha. Mind the hounds on the way out. They are not in the Guild. They will not join. We have asked.
===

title: evil_gudrun
---
Gudrun: Sit by the fire, dry your bolts. Nobody here works for the castle. Not after dark, and it is always dark.
-> Why keep an inn out here?
    Gudrun: Somebody has to keep a light on that is not looking for anybody.
    Gudrun: The castle sends a man to tell me to put the lantern out. I give him soup. He forgets what he came for.
-> Is that your face on the poster?
    Gudrun: That is yours, love. Fourth from the left. Good likeness. They got the antenna right.
-> What do you serve?
    Gudrun: Stew, ale, and the news. The stew is the most reliable.
-> Thank you, Gudrun.
    Gudrun: Mind the bog on the way out. And the hounds. And the founder, he's lying about.
===

title: evil_tobias
---
Tobias: Searchlight sweeps every eleven seconds. It lingers on the bog, it skips the old cart. That is where you walk.
-> How do you know?
    Tobias: Thirty years trapping on this moor. The lights are newer than me. I know their habits better than the men who run them.
-> What do you trap?
    Tobias: Used to be rabbits. Now it's the castle's failed prototypes. They wander off. I bring them back for the bounty, and the castle pays me in coupons for the castle.
-> What is behind the picture?
    Tobias: A picture of the castle. Lovely frame. Nothing behind it at all. Nothing that would show the blind spots of every light on the moor.
-> See you, Tobias.
    Tobias: You won't. That's the point of the blind spots.
===
